{"kind":"report","text":"LS-7 (a), per ruling c422a912: the cause of run 1's untrusted join reply, from code and the run-1 evidence only.\n\nCause: GW-1's gap, in the browser half. Lending 0.4.0 bundles the screen gateway route from before GW-1.\n- After the room records a join, `recorded()` (packages/client/src/browser-joining.ts) asks for a member session and then calls `followReceipt`. That reads the entry with `?atLeast=`.\n- The 0.4.0 bundle's `applicationGatewayRoute` allows no query on the entries read, so the screen transport throws in the browser before it sends the request. The page then reports \"No answer came back that could be trusted\" (browser-joining.ts:115). This matches run 1: the join was recorded at membership entry 8, no response had status 400 or above, and the page logged one console error.\n- Proof: Lending 0.4.0 was signed from main 7a6fcadf, where packages/client/src/application-gateway.ts has 0 `atLeast` lines. At GW-1's 830d134a it has 5. The installed screen runs presentation 188f7b84, which is 0.4.0's presentation in examples/lending/releases/0.4.0.\n- The server half is already live: GW-1 830d134a is an ancestor of the deployed 44330407.\n- NF-10 does not apply. Lending already binds the device to the service origin (main.ts:22, `serviceOrigin = screen?.origin ?? location.origin`). The NF-10 note says the same.\n\nFix route: a Lending release only, and it already exists. No platform change and no new code.\n- Lending 0.5.0 (release 1bda4e9b, signed 17 Nov from 830d134a, which contains GW-1) carries presentation 00598706. Its trust row is in APPLICATION_TRUST in apps/room/wrangler.lending.jsonc (LC-5, 4b606537).\n- 0.5.0's semantic identifier equals 0.4.0's (48616803). U3's in-place form therefore applies: `dap application upgrade 2 \u003curi\u003e --release sha256:1bda4e9b… --request \u003ckey\u003e` from the lending-shelf operator home, without --replace. The upgrade keeps item 2 and the room's journal.\n- With U3 deployed, the lending-shelf.inguz.space host serves the new presentation, because U3's matcher no longer compares the presentation. The screen address becomes …/2/sha256%3A00598706…/.\n\nOrder:\n1. You publish and deploy U3, with the rate read.\n2. The operator home runs the in-place upgrade to 0.5.0. This is your step or mine, by your word.\n3. The rerun: a second invitation, a persistent browser profile, the new screen address.\nThis also serves as a hosted witness of U3's in-place path on Lending, beside U4 on Counter.\n\nResidue for the LS-7 note: @shelf-witness, membership entry 8, key_rz2EhUy0, with no holder.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}